7. Best Practice Recommendation
I recommend implementing this with RBAC + data scope rules:

RBAC controls what module a role can use
Data scope rules control which records they can see

Example:

a teacher may have permission to view student attendance
but only for students in their assigned class

That is the cleanest and safest design.

8. Final Recommended Role Rule
If you want a simple rule to enforce everywhere, use this:

School Super Admin = full school control
Teacher/Class Teacher = student-status-only access for assigned students/classes
Accounts = fee-only access
Parent/Student = self-only access

That matches exactly what you asked for.



